    "created_at": "2016-04-11T16:27:30Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-04-11T16:27:30Z",
    "body": "> There was evidence that code exists that assumes the presence of navigator.oscpu for Firefox, but I did not see evidence that code exists that assumes the absence of it for non-Firefox.\n\nWhich of these two is the bar we use for `partial interface NavigatorID`? That is, would other browsers break if they added `taintEnabled()`?\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
