    "created_at": "2016-04-11T16:37:37Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-04-11T16:37:37Z",
    "body": "Hard to say.  https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=683151#c10 suggests that sites were using the `taintEnabled` thing to detect \"not khtml\" and then if \"khtml\" do some sorts of workarounds for bugs.  I _think_ the sniffing there, shown in https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=683151#c6, counted WebKit as \"khtml\".  So if WebKit implemented `taintEnabled` it would no longer receive the workaround.  Of course it would also break on those sites if it just fixed the bug the sites were working around... and maybe it has in the last 5 years.\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
